		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=18698#p18698"><![CDATA[
The restitution of both the colliding objects determines how much bounce there is. I think it is the product of the restitution values of the objects involved in the collision that is the determining factor.<br><br>So if you have a ball falling into a floor, both the ball and the floor should have a non-zero restitution.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6462">jarno</a> — Tue May 25, 2010 12:02 am</p><hr />
